msgctxt "professions.flavor"
msgid "Walls do not rise from loose stone alone: someone must set the courses, mix the binder, keep the tools sharp and move the crew from one site to the next. Organised building crews appear wherever towns grow — in the Nile valley, in the Andes, in the cities of Asia and in the river towns of Africa — each with its own techniques and measures. The work is often temporary, but a yard that keeps the builders and their supplies together makes every site finish sooner."
